.\" kpxcd.8 — Man page for the KeePassXC Daemon
.TH KPXCD 8 "2026-05-18" "kpxcd" "System Manager's Manual"

.SH NAME
kpxcd \- KeePassXC headless daemon for Linux

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kpxcd
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kpxcd
is a headless user-session daemon that keeps one or more KeePass databases unlocked
and available through standard Linux interprocess interfaces. It is designed for
unattended or programmatic access to passwords and SSH keys throughout
a login session, without requiring the KeePassXC GUI to be running.

Upon startup, \fBkpxcd\fR reads its configuration from
\fI~/.config/kpxcd/config.toml\fR (or the path specified with
\fB\-\-config\fR), loads any databases marked for auto-unlock, and begins
listening on the following interfaces:

.TP
.B D-Bus session bus
Exposes \fBorg.keepassxc.Daemon\fR for management operations and
\fBorg.freedesktop.secrets\fR for Secret Service compatibility.
.TP
.B Unix domain socket (SSH agent)
Listens on \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kpxcd/ssh.sock\fR and speaks the OpenSSH
agent protocol, allowing \fBssh\fR to use keys stored in the unlocked
databases.
.TP
.B Native FIDO2 (optional)
Registers a virtual CTAP2 HID authenticator through /dev/uhid. Browsers use the
kernel HID transport without extensions. Local CLI management uses D-Bus.

All sensitive data (master passwords, derived keys, decrypted entries) is held
in \fBmlock\fR(2)-ed pages and processed within secure memory scopes that zero
registers and stack on return.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config " \fIPATH\fR"
Path to the configuration file. Defaults to
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kpxcd/config.toml\fR, falling back to
\fI~/.config/kpxcd/config.toml\fR.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help message and exit.

.SH CONFIGURATION
\fBkpxcd\fR is configured via a TOML file. The full reference is in
\fBkpxcd.toml\fR(5). The configuration defines:

.RS
.TP
.B [daemon]
Global settings: idle timeout, parsed-but-unwired screen-lock option, log level, SSH mode.
.TP
.B [[database]]
One or more database entries: path, auto-unlock behavior, credential source,
SSH key exposure.
.TP
.B [secret_service]
Secret Service D-Bus settings: enable/disable, notifications, Polkit
confirmation.
.TP
.B [ssh_agent]
SSH agent settings: enable/disable and parsed-but-unenforced lifetime/confirm-on-use.
.TP
.B [fido2]
Native UHID authenticator and implemented local passkey APIs; disabled by default.
Browser generation is ES256; existing local ES256/EdDSA signing remains available.
.RE

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kpxcd/config.toml
Default configuration file. See \fBkpxcd.toml\fR(5).

.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kpxcd/ssh.sock
Unix domain socket for the SSH agent protocol. Permissions: 0600.

.TP
.I /dev/uhid
Kernel interface for the optional native FIDO2 device; requires module and device
permissions in an approved deployment.

.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.keepassxc.daemon.policy
Polkit policy file defining authorization requirements for sensitive operations.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides the default configuration directory. If set, the config file is
sought at \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kpxcd/config.toml\fR.

.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory for runtime files (sockets). Must be set and must be a per-user,
per-session directory. Defaults to \fI/run/user/$UID\fR.

.TP
.B CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY
If set (by systemd \fBLoadCredential=\fR), \fBkpxcd\fR reads auto-unlock
passwords from \fI$CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY/<credential-name>\fR.

.TP
.B SSH_AUTH_SOCK
Used when \fBssh_mode = "proxy"\fR. \fBkpxcd\fR forwards agent requests to
the socket specified here.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Start the daemon with the default config:
.nf
    kpxcd
.fi

.TP
.B Start with a custom config file:
.nf
    kpxcd --config /etc/kpxcd/my-config.toml
.fi

.TP
.B Run as a systemd user service:
.nf
    systemctl --user enable --now kpxcd.service
.fi

.TP
.B Check if the daemon is running:
.nf
    kpxcctl ping
.fi

.SH BUGS
Report bugs at the project repository.

Known limitations:
.RS
.TP
.B Passkey persistence and compatibility
Registration and signing write credentials/counters. Explicit resident
same-account replacement is selected-destination-only, checks unlocked databases,
and refuses multiple or cross-database matches. Unrelated entry fields are retained;
there is no migration. Locked/unopened matches are invisible. Optimistic external
file conflict detection is not a cross-process transaction guarantee.
Historical wrong user handles generally cannot be repaired; only affected
credentials may need separately approved re-registration. Imported transport hints
excluding USB cannot be changed by local import. Amazon diagnosis is unconfirmed.
.TP
.B Native identity and approval
The fixed product AAGUID is ab449b5e-d0bf-4d8d-81b1-de5ec1a8c00e.
Deprecated aaguid, algorithms and user_verification config keys load but warn and
are ignored. Native approval assumes fresh auth_self authentication; cached or
locally overridden policy can invalidate UP/UV claims. zdr is only an optional
agent example. One unix:path or unix:abstract system-bus address is supported.
Cancellation attempts same-connection polkit cleanup but cannot recall an entered
output write or roll back completed persistence. See doc/passkeys.md.
.TP
.B Verification status
Current live kernel, host polkit security and Chrome/Firefox browser checks are
NOT RUN/awaiting approval. Synthetic envelopes and fake authorization tests are
not live compatibility/security evidence. No FIDO certification is claimed.

.TP
.B Cold boot attacks
\fBmlock\fR prevents swap-out but does not prevent DRAM retention attacks.
Use encrypted swap and LUKS for full disk encryption.

.TP
.B Root compromise
\fBkpxcd\fR does not defend against a compromised root account. This is
consistent with the Linux security model.
.RE

.SH AUTHOR
kpxcd was written as a standalone project. It shares no code with KeePassXC.

